\u093f\u0924 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0907\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u0915\u094b \u0905\u092a\u0928\u093e \u092c\u093e\u0939\u094d\u092f\u0924\u092e \u0915\u094b\u0936 \u092a\u0942\u0930\u093e \u0915\u0930\u0928\u0947 \u0915\u0947 \u0932\u093f\u090f \u0915\u0947\u0935\u0932 \u090f\u0915 \u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0915\u0940 \u0906\u0935\u0936\u094d\u092f\u0915\u0924\u093e \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f \u092f\u0947 \u090f\u0915 \u0905\u0924\u093f\u0930\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0924 \u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0915\u094b \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092c\u0932\u0924\u093e \u0938\u0947 \u0906\u0915\u0930\u094d\u0937\u093f\u0924 \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964 \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0907\u0928\u0915\u0940 \u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0932\u092c\u094d\u0927\u093f \u090f\u0928\u094d\u0925\u0948\u0932\u094d\u092a\u0940 (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.669ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.279ex\" height=\"2.289ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 2333.5 1011.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"65\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-65\"></use><use data-c=\"67\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-67\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) \u0915\u093e \u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0927\u093f\u0915 \u090b\u0923\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u0915 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":144000,"topic":"periodic-table-and-its-features","type":"mcq","year":2026,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2026-online-6th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>lowest and lowest</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>highest and lowest</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>lowest and highest</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>highest and highest</p>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The element on the far left of a period belongs to Group 1. These elements have only one electron in their outermost shell, so they lose this electron easily. Therefore, they have the lowest first ionisation enthalpy (IE).</p>\n<p>The element on the far right of a period, except noble gases, belongs to Group 17 (halogens). These atoms need just one electron to complete their outermost shell, so they strongly attract an extra electron. Hence, they have the most negative value of electron gain enthalpy (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.669ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.279ex\" height=\"2.289ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 2333.5 1011.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"65\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-65\"></use><use data-c=\"67\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-67\" transform=\"translate(444,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</p>","qKey":"pin-a-period-the-first-ionisation-enthalpy-of-the-element-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-20vzkxznn2ovktwe","paperKey":"jee-main-2026-online-6th-april-evening-shift"}]}